    "result_text": "All 22 test classes (33 tests) pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the `bulkSignupWarning` field: **true when more than 80 owners were already created today, otherwise false**, following the same \"created today\" accumulation path as the existing daily-create-limit rule (owners whose adjusted business-day `registrationDate` equals today's business day).\n\nChanges made:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `bulkSignupWarning` boolean property to the `Owner` schema (regenerates `OwnerDto`).\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added the persistent `bulkSignupWarning` field (`@Column(name = \"bulk_signup_warning\")`) with getter/setter, so it's carried through to the GET response, mirroring how `namesakeCount`/`customerCode` work. MapStruct auto-maps it by name.\n\n3. **`AssignBulkSignupWarning.java`** (new function) \u2014 counts existing owners registered on today's business day and sets the flag to `count > 80`, before save so the count excludes the new owner.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step between `assignCode` and `save`, under `govern: [ transaction ]`.\n\n5. **Schema/data SQL** \u2014 added the `bulk_signup_warning` column to all four `schema.sql` dialects (hsqldb/h2/postgres/mysql) and appended the extra positional `NULL` to the 10 seed-owner inserts in the hsqldb `data.sql` (the only file using positional inserts; the others use explicit column lists).\n\nThe Cp22 test creates a fresh owner and GETs it, asserting `bulkSignupWarning` is `false` \u2014 which now passes, and the full suite stays green.",
